{"study_accession":"PRJNA698389","secondary_study_accession":"SRP304033","title":"Bulk RNA-seq of aplastic anemia (AA) and healthy donors","description":"Bulk RNA-seq data of Lin-CD34+ hematopoietic stem and progenitor cells derived from bone marrow of healthy donors and untreated aplastic anemia patients Overall design: Mononuclear cells from 3 healthy donors and untreated aplastic anemia patients' bone marrow aspirates were isolated using Ficoll density gradient separation and cryopreserved in 90% FBS/ 10% DMSO for storage in liquid nitrogen. The thawing frozen cells were stained with human antibodies including lineage cocktail (CD3, CD14, CD16, CD19, CD20, CD56) (BV510, Biolegend) and CD34 (APC, Clone 581, BD Biosciences) antibodies. Lin-CD34+ HSPCs (cell count ranges from 130 to 2000) were sorted directly into cell lysis buffer on a BD FACSAria III. The reverse transcription and template switch steps were performed following the full-length Smart-seq2 protocol with some modifications. Concentration of oligd(T30VN) and template switch oligo (TSO) primers used for mRNA reverse transcription were double. The cDNA was fragmented using Covaris S220 instead of Tn5 transposase. The processes of end repair, polyA-tailing, adaptor ligation and library amplification were using KAPA Hyper Prep Kits (Kapa Biosystems, Cat# KK8504) and NEBNext Multiplex Oligos for Illumina (Index Primers Set 1) (NEB, Cat# E7335L).The 150bp paired-end reads were generated from Illumina NovaSeq6000 platform. For data processing, TSO primer, polyA tail, adaptor, and low-quality sequence (N > 10%) were trimmed using Trimmomatic (version 0.36). Clean reads were aligned against the human GRCh38 genome using STAR (version 2.7)). Duplicate reads were identified and removed by using Picard(version 2.17.6). MATS(version 4.0.2) and DaPars(version 0.9.0) to perform alternative splicing and alternative polyadenylation analysis, respectively. Gene quantification was using HTSeq (version 0.9.1).","pubmed":"33763704","geo_series":"","n_samples":9,"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN17717332","study_accession":"PRJNA698389","blood_class":"bone_marrow","class_from":"sample","title":"P23","description":"P23","sex":"female","geo_sample":"GSM5051842","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2021-04-01","attributes":[["source_name","P23"],["sex","female"],["disease","non-SAA"],["surface markers","Lin-CD34+"],["tissue","Bone Marrow"],["age","33"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR13593594","experiment_accession":"SRX9988102","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":19851120,"base_count":5955336000,"first_public":"2021-04-01","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: GSM5051842: P23 Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":true},{"sample_accession":"SAMN17717333","study_accession":"PRJNA698389","blood_class":"bone_marrow","class_from":"sample","title":"P22","description":"P22","sex":"male","geo_sample":"GSM5051841","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2021-04-01","attributes":[["source_name","P22"],["sex","male"],["disease","non-SAA"],["surface markers","Lin-CD34+"],["tissue","Bone Marrow"],["age","32"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR13593593","experiment_accession":"SRX9988101","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":22559881,"base_count":6767964300,"first_public":"2021-04-01","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: GSM5051841: P22 Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":true},{"sample_accession":"SAMN17717334","study_accession":"PRJNA698389","blood_class":"bone_marrow","class_from":"sample","title":"P21","description":"P21","sex":"female","geo_sample":"GSM5051840","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2021-04-01","attributes":[["source_name","P21"],["sex","female"],["disease","non-SAA"],["surface markers","Lin-CD34+"],["tissue","Bone Marrow"],["age","40"]]